ue="1000000"><text:p>1000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>military</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1"><text:p>1</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000"><text:p>1000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>military</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="2"><text:p>2</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="10000"><text:p>10000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>military</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="3"><text:p>3</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000000"><text:p>1000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>metalwork</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1"><text:p>1</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000"><text:p>1000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>metalwork</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="2"><text:p>2</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="10000"><text:p>10000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>metalwork</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="3"><text:p>3</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000000"><text:p>1000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row></table:table><table:table table:name="Ages"><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Ages</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell/><table:table-cell/></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>index</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>age</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>population threshold</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="0"><text:p>0</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Ancient</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="0"><text:p>0</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1"><text:p>1</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Iron Age</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000"><text:p>1000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="2"><text:p>2</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Classical</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="10000"><text:p>10000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="3"><text:p>3</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Middle Ages</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000000"><text:p>1000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="4"><text:p>4</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Renaissance</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="100000000"><text:p>100000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="5"><text:p>5</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Industrial</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="1000000000"><text:p>1000000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="6"><text:p>6</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Modern / Space</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="float" office:value="10000000000"><text:p>10000000000</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row></table:table><table:table table:name="Notes"><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>How to read this workbook</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p></text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Plan</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>one row per citizen milestone (10 … 10 B). (model) columns are formulas over Inputs + Data; (engine) columns are values read from the real game engine for the assumed build. Change an Inputs value to re-price the model columns — the engine columns stay as measured.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Targets</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>one row per milestone × building: the next unit's cost, the capacity limit and the time to afford it at that milestone's rates.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Assumed build</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>houses = citizens / Inputs.citizensPerHouse; town halls = houses / Inputs.housesPerTownHall; every other building = citizens / its ratio, rounded up. The engine is measured with exactly these counts, so the engine and model columns start in agreement.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Workers</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>citizens × the worker-share inputs, rounded down. Each worker produces 1/s (food, wood, stone, gold) or 0.1/s (science).</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Production (engine)</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>the engine's own rate: (Σ flat) × (Π multipliers) − (Σ drain). Food carries the citizen upkeep, −1/s per citizen.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Multiplier columns</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>building × = the building's own per-unit factor ^ count; achievement × = the ‹resource›-multiplier chain tiers unlocked by that building count; upgrade × = ×2 per enhancer tier passed; other × = research + battle + age bonuses (engine values — edit them to test a different research pace).</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Times</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>next building = the slowest of its cost resources (unit cost / that resource's production). Next research = 100 × 2.5^purchases science. 'Time incl. research' takes the slower of the two, because science and resources accrue in parallel.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Approximations</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>upgrades are assumed bought as soon as their building-count threshold is met; research is assumed bought for every earlier age (Inputs.boughtResearchShare trims that); battles are assumed won for every earlier age; resources are assumed held at exactly the next purchase's cost, which is what unlocks the hoarder tiers.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>Reading the balance</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>the engine columns are the current data's answer, not a target. Where they explode or stall is what to tune — start with the cost factors on Data and the ratios on Inputs.</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row></table:table></office:spreadsheet></office:body></office:document>